# Build outputs + deps rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
# tsc -b incremental state. MUST be excluded alongside dist/: if a stale
# .tsbuildinfo from a developer's working tree is copied in while dist/ is not,
# `tsc -b` sees "already built" and emits nothing, leaving packages/*/dist
# empty — and the web vite build then fails to resolve @patch/wire. Excluding
# it keeps the image build reproducible from a clean checkout (spec/11).
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
.vite
coverage
.pnpm-store

# Python voice sidecar venvs/caches — rebuilt by `uv venv` in the image.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Local dev + model artifacts (mounted at runtime, not baked in).
.dev-data
.dev-data-*
.tmp
models
*.log
.DS_Store

# Runtime data written BY the containers (root-owned) — must not be in the build
# context (unreadable files break `docker build`'s context scan) and must never
# be baked into an image.
data
deploy/data
**/.patch

# Published artifacts served BY the box (daemon tarballs, APKs, desktop builds).
# They live under the deploy dir on the host and are 2.7 GB and growing: pulling
# them into the build context copied every one of them into the builder for a
# `COPY . .`, which is what filled the disk and broke `pnpm ship server` with
# "no space left on device" — while building nothing that needs them.
deploy/downloads
